Inka Markdown writes a value that isn't plain text as a bound attribute, as Vue does: `:levels="3"`, `:styles='{"align":"left"}'`, `:facets="[]"`, and a block tag names its type with `is` (`<block is="inPageAlert" type="info">`), leaving `type` free for a field. A block with a list, object or `type` field keeps its Markdown instead of becoming a JSON blob. The old forms (`levels=3`, `styles:align="left"`, `<block type="…">`) are refused; migrate content by re-exporting it. @djay
